From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:43:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Floor a fixed-layout border-box cell width at its padding and
 border
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fixed table layout took a first-row cell's border-box width as its
column width even when the cell's horizontal padding and border were
wider. The cell box cannot be narrower than its padding and border, so
it overflowed its column and overlapped the next one: a 20px-wide
border-box cell with 23px of padding started the next column 3px inside
itself. A click at the centre of a control in that next cell then hit
the following cell instead, and the cells' client rects overlapped.

Browsers floor the column width at the cell's padding plus border, as
they already do in effect for content-box cells, which add both to the
width. Do the same for border-box cells.

beep-boop-🤖
---
 src/layout/table.rs | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/layout/table.rs b/src/layout/table.rs
index 892be74..225394d 100644
--- a/src/layout/table.rs
+++ b/src/layout/table.rs
@@ -788,7 +788,11 @@ fn collect_table_cells(
                             taffy::BoxSizing::ContentBox => style_helpers::length(
                                 len + padding.left + padding.right + border.left + border.right,
                             ),
-                            taffy::BoxSizing::BorderBox => style_helpers::length(len),
+                            // The cell box cannot shrink below its padding and border, so a
+                            // narrower column would let it overlap the next column's cells.
+                            taffy::BoxSizing::BorderBox => style_helpers::length(
+                                len.max(padding.left + padding.right + border.left + border.right),
+                            ),
                         }
                     }
                     taffy::CompactLength::PERCENT_TAG => {
